KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ no copies: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ each object destroyed once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.init.general]/16.6.1, [class.temporary]/2, [stmt.return]/2: in
C++17 a prvalue of the class type initializes the result object directly
(`D x = D(4)', `D y = make(5)', `A a{make(6)}', array elements), so the
copy constructor is not called and no temporary is destroyed.  The front
end materializes a temporary, copies it and destroys it: the state is
right for a faithful copy constructor, but side effects of copy
constructors and destructors are counted wrongly.  Also fails on bin53.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
